25.4. Integration
Trapezoidal Rule
25.4.1
\int_{x_{0}}^{x_{1}}f(x)dx=\frac{h}{2}(f_{0}+f_{1})-\frac{1}{2}\int_{x_{0}}^{x_{1}}(t-z_{0})(x_{1}-t)f^{\prime\prime}(t)dt=\frac{h}{2}(f_{0}+f_{1})-\frac{h^{3}}{12}f^{\prime\prime}(\xi)(x_{0}<k<z_{1}) Extended Trapezoidal Rule
25.4.2
\int_{x_{0}}^{x_{m}}f(x)dx=h\left[\frac{f_{0}}{2}+f_{1}+\ldots+f_{m-1}+\frac{f_{m}}{2}\right]-\frac{mk^{3}}{12}f^{\prime\prime}(\xi)
Error Term in Trapezoidal Formula for Periodic Functions
If f(x) is periodic and has a continuous kth derivative, and if the integral is taken over a period, then
25.4.3
|Error|<=\frac{\text{constant}}{m^{k}} Modified Trapezoidal Rule
